  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 214 PM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nThe axis of the upper level ridge is forecast to shift slightly \nto the east on Thursday centered near the Arizona/New Mexico\nborder. This puts west central Texas in northerly flow aloft.\nModels continue to show a shortwave trough rounding the edge of\nthe aforementioned ridge. Have continued the mention of a low to\nmedium chance (20-40%) of isolated to scattered showers and \nthunderstorms mainly Wednesday night into Thursday afternoon. The\nprimary hazards with these storms would be gusty winds and brief\nheavy rainfall. With chances for rain and increased cloud cover we\nmay finally see temperatures 'only' in the upper 90s as opposed \nto widespread triple digits. By the weekend, however, the upper \nridge builds back to the east bringing a return to hot and dry \nconditions.",
